{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>הראת.</b> From a binyan whose verbal noun is not named. The sense: כי כל אלה הראך האלהים עד אשר תדע כי הוא האלהים לבדו (for all these, Elohim showed you, so that you may know that He alone is Elohim)." "And the sense of <b>אין עוד</b> (there is none else): as I hinted in the commentary on Ecclesiastes at the verse וגבוהים עליהם (and higher than they), therefore the word אין עוד." "And the word Elohim I explained in the pericope of וישמע יתרו, in כתוב וידבר אלהים, and האלהים יעננו בקול, in בא האלהים, where the name HaElohim is placed — for the one speaking is Elohim. For there is one who will not understand in abbreviated fashion, and it is a deep sod."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:21.415827346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}